  "action": "Compared Netra Runtime pricing vs official DeepSeek api.deepseek.com (deepseek-flash / DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash). Netra flat: .20 input / .05 cached / .50 output per 1M. OG has peak/off-peak split (peak 01:00-04:00 + 06:00-10:00 UTC weekdays): off-peak .15/.003/.60, peak .30/.006/.20. Netra wins on output (flat .50 beats .60/.20). OG wins decisively on cached input - 8-17x cheaper (.003-0.006 vs .05); OG discounts cache ~50x off fresh vs Netra's 4x. For the user's cache-heavy 65k-context agent loops OG is ~5x cheaper per turn. Corrected earlier framing that overstated Netra's cache advantage. Noted Netra's flat pricing benefits Indonesian WIB timezone since OG peak hours = 08:00-11:00 and 13:00-17:00 WIB."
